  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Review the Sample Project\r\n\r\nTo the right is a sample student project, Mood Playlist Picker, shown the way it would appear in Web Lab.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Click through the file tabs (`planning.md`, `index.html`, `style.css`, `script.js`, `reflection.md`) to review each piece of evidence.\r\n2. Click **Preview** to see the actual working app. Try clicking Happy, Chill, and Sad.\r\n3. On the left, click each rubric category to expand it and read all four tiers.\r\n4. For each category, click the tier you think best describes this project. Your selection will highlight, and a running score will update at the bottom of the rubric panel.\r\n5. You can change your answer at any time, this is practice, not a test.",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "true",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "predict_settings": {
